cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the IIP-TF converter, please cite this software. If you use
  converted inscription data, also cite the Brown University Library
  Inscriptions of Israel/Palestine project (https://doi.org/10.26300/pz1d-st89)
  and the scholarly editions credited by the original records. The upstream
  corpus is not covered by the converter's MIT license.
type: software
title: 'IIP-TF: Text-Fabric converter for the Inscriptions of Israel/Palestine'
authors:
  - family-names: Sosnovshchenko
    given-names: Oleksandr
version: '0.1.0.dev0'
abstract: >-
  IIP-TF converts Brown University Library's Inscriptions of Israel/Palestine
  EpiDoc source corpus into a research-oriented Text-Fabric dataset. The
  converter is in pre-release development; upstream corpus data and scholarly
  editions retain their own licenses and attribution requirements.
repository-code: https://github.com/alexsosn/IIP-TF
url: https://github.com/alexsosn/IIP-TF
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Text-Fabric
  - EpiDoc
  - epigraphy
  - inscriptions
